Upstream adds id to an existing *://*/* rule (the DR-F10 hole: the rule
already exists, the pair is new): Risky fails; passes with an ack bound to
the new bytes; fails again with that ack expired.
-- ops --
jappend rules/brave/clean-urls.json [{"include": "*://*/*"}, "params"] "id"
relock
run Risky
fail Risky: new global pair (global, id): id is a risky name (never-strip)
-- head/rules/acks.json --
{"schema": 1, "acks": [
  {"check": "risky", "scope": "global", "param": "id",
   "vendored_sha256": "${sha:rules/brave/clean-urls.json}", "expires": "2026-12-01",
   "reason": "fixture: accepted after review", "by": "fixture"}
], "holds": []}
-- ops --
run Risky
pass
log acked by fixture
now 2026-12-02
run Risky
fail Risky: new global pair (global, id)
log ack expired (2026-12-01)
